<#
.SYNOPSIS
    Collects Microsoft 365 audit evidence, analyzes suspicious activity, and creates a tabbed HTML report.

.DESCRIPTION
    Read-only investigation script derived from the startup and connection workflow in the supplied
    mailbox health script. It validates the local environment, installs/imports required modules,
    supports regular or delegated tenant sign-in, connects to Exchange Online, Microsoft Purview,
    and Microsoft Graph, and continues in partial mode when a workload is unavailable.

    Evidence sources:
      - Microsoft Purview Unified Audit Log
      - Exchange Online administrator audit log
      - Microsoft Entra sign-in logs
      - Microsoft Entra directory audit logs
      - Microsoft Entra provisioning logs
      - Microsoft Entra ID Protection risk detections and risky users
      - Microsoft Entra Conditional Access policy configuration
      - Microsoft Defender XDR alerts and incidents through Microsoft Graph Security
      - Azure subscription Activity Logs and subscription diagnostic settings
      - Microsoft Secure Score history, control results, and control profiles
      - Audit configuration and retention metadata

    The report contains separate analysis tabs and separate raw-data tabs for every collector,
    source-by-source retention and enablement details, and progress/status estimates.
    Every source is permission/licensing dependent. "Unavailable" is reported explicitly and is
    never treated as an empty or healthy result.

.NOTES
    Version: 3.0.0
    Platform: Windows PowerShell 5.1 Desktop
    Authentication: Interactive delegated authentication only; no passwords or secrets are stored.
    Safety: Read-only. No tenant, mailbox, security, audit, or policy setting is changed.
    Regression baseline: Supplied test output successfully collected UAL, Entra, Conditional Access,
    Defender Alerts, Secure Score History, and 460 Secure Score Control Profiles. The report records
    these expectations without treating a changing cloud control-profile count as a fatal error.
    Azure isolation: Az.Accounts is never imported into the parent Graph/Exchange/Purview process.
#>

